// Trade (milestone 2, step 5).
// Links: each settlement links to the linksPerSettlement settlements it can reach most cheaply
// over land, within maxLinkCost. Crossing one cell costs 1 on lowland, more on hills and
// mountains, and riverFactor times as much where both cells are on a river (a cell is about
// 51 km). Seas and lakes are not crossed. A link counts if either end chose it.
// Trade: each month, along each link, a good moves from the cheaper end to the dearer end if
// the price gap is larger than the carrying cost (the good's weight times costPerStep food for
// each unit of link cost). The cheaper end sends sendShare of its stock of that good each
// month, scaled down when the gap only just beats the cost. Goods arrive the next month.
// A trade route is a link whose carried value (in food) averages at least routeValue a month.
{
  "maxLinkCost": 4.0,
  "linksPerSettlement": 6,
  "terrainCost": { "lowland": 1.0, "hills": 1.6, "mountains": 3.0 },
  "riverFactor": 0.5,
  "costPerStep": 0.02,
  "sendShare": 0.05,
  "routeValue": 1.0
}
